    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0590" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00111 Armament Control—Military
                    Secrets/3574</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-24">October 24, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Murray</hi>: I agree completely with the opinion
                    expressed in the last paragraph of your memorandum.<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d489-f1"/> Please see the Greek Minister for me and take care to
                    explain to him that our present situation makes it impossible, after full
                    consideration, for us to do anything in the way of assistance to Greece through
                    supplying airplanes for some time to come.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
